Author:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Fri Oct 23 20:15:21 2026 -0500
Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Fri Oct 23 20:15:21 2026 -0500

    fix: seed preserves corpus created_at timestamps
    
    The seed loader re-stamped every imported row with the seed run's wall
    clock via the SQLite DEFAULT (datetime('now')), discarding the corpus's
    own created_at values. New classes and answers now store the corpus
    timestamp; rows that already exist are never rewritten, so a re-run
    leaves every stored created_at byte-identical.
    
    - internal/graph: createProblemClass/createAnswerNode and their upsert
      wrapper take a createdAt parameter, inserted via
      COALESCE(NULLIF(?, ''), datetime('now')) so an empty value degrades to
      the schema default — one statement for both arms, no drift between
      the standalone and batched (Tx) paths. The existing public signatures
      are unchanged (174 call sites); the timestamped entry points are the
      additive CreateProblemClassAt / UpsertProblemClassAt /
      CreateAnswerNodeAt variants on Store and Tx.
    - internal/seed: seedFile passes cf.CreatedAt / ans.CreatedAt through
      the new Tx variants. Answer dedup identity is now
      (env, lang, version, solution, created_at): the corpus holds re-solve
      snapshots that share the content tuple and differ only in when they
      were written, and collapsing them dropped the newer snapshot (e.g.
      serde-json-validator-jsonschema's two answers). A corpus answer with
      no created_at still dedups on the plain content tuple, so legacy
      files stay idempotent against default-stamped rows.
    - Tests: TestSeedPreservesCorpusCreatedAt pins corpus stamps on classes
      and answers, the snapshot-pair shape, the default-stamp fallback, and
      re-run byte-stability; TestCreatedAtExplicitVsDefault pins the
      store-level arms including upsert-never-rewrites; the
      across-databases determinism dump now includes created_at for
      problem_classes and answer_nodes (loader output, not wall clock).
    
    Verified: go build ./...; go vet; go test ./... -count=1 (all ok);
    fresh seed of the 2863-file corpus → 2863 distinct class timestamps,
    serde-json-validator-jsonschema class stamped 2026-07-25 01:10:08 with
    answers 2026-07-25 01:10:08 and 2026-10-01 07:20:47 in id order;
    re-run creates 0 rows and leaves all query outputs byte-identical.
    
    Addresses DF-OFF-BY-ONE-58.
